Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-10-2000||03:38 PM||||Got the car going yesterday.  Had some heating problems at first.  Turned out the fan fuse had blown and the fan wasn't going so when I got into traffic it over heated. I had forgotten that when you reconnect the battery in my car to pull fuses before making everything hot. Which was good then we found that the intake manifold need new gaskets.  Pulled that and resealed in 2 -3 hours.  Got it back on the road and ran about half a tank out driving til about 2 AM.  It is awesome.  It runs like a champ.  It's fast looks good and sounds mean.  I'm takin a drive again in a few minutes to go back to the shop for some adjustments.  Thanks to everyone who helped with advice.  Thanks Bob Sato master mechanic. Thanks most of all to the geniius of V8 Archie for figuring out how to put one of the most awesome driving packages together that I have ever driven.  Wohoo gotta go drive.  I'll post pictures and details as soon as I've driven to my hearts' content.  Wife what wife?||||reg||6
Z||000001||deceler8||11-10-2000||04:03 PM||||Cool. The only thing better than having a V8 Fiero is having one in Hawaii.<P>||||reg||1
